# Source-distribution contents.
#
# setuptools' default sdist heuristic picks up top-level *.py files and
# stops, so the published sdist used to carry 9 of the repo's test modules
# and none of the machinery that runs them - no conftest.py, no
# tests/__init__.py, no tests/fuzz/, no tests/simulator/. `pytest` in the
# unpacked artifact therefore collected nothing and errored on
# `from tests.conftest import ...`.
#
# A downstream packager, an auditor, or a distribution's build system takes
# the *sdist*, so advertising a suite it cannot execute is worse than
# shipping none. This ships the whole thing: with the `dev` extra installed
# (which is what the shipped `addopts = "-n auto"` needs), `pytest` in the
# unpacked sdist runs the same suite CI does.
#
# `.github/workflows/test.yml`'s `packaging` job unpacks the built sdist and
# asserts this choice, so it cannot drift back silently.
graft tests
graft docs
include CHANGELOG.md
include uv.lock

# Nothing generated, cached, or internal.
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude .coverage*
prune tests/__pycache__
prune .hypothesis
prune .claude
